            "subject": "Stop retrying requests the server already refused",
            "body": "Stop retrying requests the server already refused\n\nretry: 2 applied to every failure, including 4xx. A 403 or 404 is a decision\nthe server will repeat identically, so each screen load fired three of them —\nnoticed as three consecutive 403s from GET /recurring on an unconfirmed\naccount.\n\nNetwork failures and 5xx still retry twice, which is what the setting was for\non mobile connections.\n\nConsidered exempting 408 and 429 and deliberately did not: an axios timeout\nraises ECONNABORTED with no response, so it never arrives as a 408, and\nretrying a 429 within React Query's ~1-2s backoff cannot outlast a rack-attack\nwindow — it only spends more requests against the limit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
            "author": {
